<title>USA: Vectra Banking Corp Q1 net increases.</title>
<headline>Vectra Banking Corp Q1 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the quarters ended</p>
<p>					  Mar 31,   Dec. 31,    Mar 31,</p>
<p>					    1997	 1996	 1996</p>
<p> Net interest income		  6,555	6,573	4,469</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses	    230	  309	  179</p>
<p>  Gain on sale of loans		 230	  364	  390</p>
<p>Net gain/(loss) on sale of securities</p>
<p>					     (31)	 (34)	    0</p>
<p> Net earnings			   1,672	1,688	  989</p>
<p> Preferred stock dividend	     377	  384	  185</p>
<p>Net earnings available to common</p>
<p>  shareholders			  1,295	1,304	  804</p>
<p>Earnings per average common share</p>
<p>outstanding:</p>
<p> Primary earnings per share	  0.39	 0.40	 0.25</p>
<p>Average common shares and</p>
<p>  equivalents outstanding     3,312,327  3,293,053  3,254,885</p>
<p> Earnings per fully diluted share  0.36	 0.37	 0.25</p>
<p>Fully diluted common shares</p>
<p>  outstanding		     4,140,319  4,121,045  3,254,885</p>
<p>(Dollars in thousands, except share and per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Net income was calculated before the payment of preferred dividends, earnings per share were calculated after the payment of preferred dividends.</p>
<p>The first quarter of 1997 includes the results of Southwest State Bank, which was acquired in June 1996.</p>
</text>
